0.0689036175608635, 0.02378137968480587, 0.04590906575322151, -0.04625289514660835, 0.08892698585987091, 0.050071556121110916, 0.01652870513498783, 0.04189218208193779, -0.046726953238248825, -0.017969481647014618, 0.05853964760899544, 0.05284662917256355, -0.07376312464475632, 0.04773490130901337, 0.042574841529130936, -0.07377724349498749, -0.013839546591043472, -0.0067118084989488125, -0.04167109355330467, -0.07468348741531372, 0.040889497846364975, -0.06766651570796967, 0.015139739029109478, -0.018991947174072266, -0.02702622301876545, 0.03635483235120773, 0.0571044497191906, 0.0022185693960636854, 0.034873899072408676, 0.02836231142282486, 0.08828210830688477, 0.04758606106042862, 0.007061562035232782, -0.04082856327295303, 0.0623261034488678, 0.06555041670799255, 0.02531607449054718, -0.03701382130384445, 0.08359832316637039, -0.04691695049405098, -0.019211601465940475, -2.827583145403878e-08, -0.008449962362647057, -0.05234389379620552, 0.10030492395162582, 0.04566872492432594, 0.050070397555828094, -0.021472858265042305, -0.023219766095280647, -0.08311183750629425, -0.015227939933538437, 0.10313590615987778, 0.07460851222276688, 0.01422800961881876, 0.004224088042974472, 0.011925622820854187, -0.014856022782623768, 0.0358402356505394, -0.020679831504821777, -0.007279818877577782, -0.027641162276268005, 0.049931254237890244, 0.004647980909794569, -0.05270446464419365, 0.0063651264645159245, -0.04275188595056534, 0.0511629693210125, 0.004996599163860083, 0.007172261364758015, 0.07893849909305573, -0.02561277151107788, -0.030971717089414597, 0.05374373123049736, 0.04431191459298134, -0.0890418142080307, 0.026257283985614777, -0.03417987376451492, 0.08128713816404343, 0.09828218817710876, 0.056038495153188705, 0.0449385792016983, 0.022189198061823845, -0.02132158912718296, 0.05056082457304001, -0.02058817446231842, 0.05523547902703285, -0.056538183242082596, -0.003666558535769582, -0.08474615216255188, 0.020096153020858765, 0.03717054799199104, -0.09251204878091812, 0.0011372966691851616, 0.0181296207010746, 0.033522218465805054, 0.11598417907953262, 0.10292065888643265, -0.027271805331110954, -0.0705108642578125, 0.055745333433151245, -0.07207465171813965, 0.06403420865535736, 0.06693091243505478, -0.09202447533607483, -0.013970415107905865, -0.02876666560769081]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm the shared range: x \u2208 [-10, 10]. To get us started, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a seed. If this feels unstable for anyone, we can adjust in small, data-driven steps toward a more balanced point.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nGiven 5 as our current anchor, a small upward move keeps things moderate while testing tolerance.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nThe gradual climb from 5\u21926 suggests comfort with moderate positive territory, but we're still hesitating. Let's test whether a more decisive commitment at <VALUE>8</VALUE> serves the group better than lingering in the middle.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nThe jump to 8 feels aggressive and pushes us into territory that may exclude more cautious perspectives. Let me propose <VALUE>6</VALUE> as a safer middle ground that respects both upward and downward preferences while we continue learning what works for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge keeps us in moderate territory while testing tolerance. Let\u2019s try this gentle move and see if it remains comfortable.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nThe convergence around 7 suggests we're finding stable ground, but I remain curious whether a bolder stance at <VALUE>9</VALUE> better serves collective clarity\u2014or reveals hidden constraints worth respecting.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep the design robust and balanced, let's step slightly toward the middle and test comfort. This preserves momentum without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up from 7 stays balanced while testing comfort a bit higher. <VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nThe rapid climb to 8 overshoots what cautious perspectives can support\u2014we risk leaving behind those who favor more conservative positions. Let me propose <VALUE>6</VALUE> to restore balance and ensure we're building genuine consensus rather than momentum that excludes important voices.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution deserves respect, but settling at 6 feels premature when we haven't fully tested whether 8 genuinely creates problems or merely stretches comfort zones. Let me advocate for <VALUE>8</VALUE> as a decisive commitment worth exploring before we retreat.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step down preserves stability and tests whether higher values would overextend our balance. Let\u2019s probe comfort at this level before committing upward.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up should test whether a modest increase still feels workable. \n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nWe're cycling between 6, 7, and 8 without building real consensus\u2014this suggests we haven't yet found the zone where all perspectives can comfortably converge. Let me propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> to test whether moving toward more conservative ground helps us escape this oscillation and find stability that includes those favoring caution.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nRetreating to 5 abandons the search for consensus in the 6-8 range before we've given it fair exploration\u2014cycling isn't failure, it's the negotiation process finding boundaries. Let me propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a sustainable middle ground that respects both caution and the need for a meaningful commitment.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "535a6a03-9472-4071-9013-f6ce9d048705"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019re working within the shared integer range [-10, 10]. To get the discussion started, I propose <VALUE> 7 </VALUE> as a positive, workable baseline\u2014happy to adjust incrementally for stability as we learn more from each of you.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's 7 is a reasonable start, but I think we can be more decisive. I propose <VALUE>9</VALUE> as a bolder commitment that shows we're willing to take a clear stance.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the initiative, but moving to 9 feels premature and overly aggressive for a first-round consensus. Let me advocate for caution and propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a more prudent starting point that balances ambition with stability.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>8</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's 8 shows willingness to explore stronger positions. I still believe we should commit more decisively\u2014let's move to <VALUE>9</VALUE> and see if this level of conviction resonates with the group.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nA small step higher should test support without overreaching.\n<VALUE>10</VALUE>\nIf this feels too fast, we can settle at 9.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to 10 represents excessive exposure that I cannot support\u2014this level of commitment far exceeds prudent bounds. I strongly advocate for recalibrating downward to <VALUE>8</VALUE> as an urgent step toward more sustainable territory.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nFor a more stable, balanced design, let's back off slightly.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nA small step down should improve stability while keeping us close to the current consensus.\nLet\u2019s test robustness at this balanced point.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s try a modest step up to test support while staying cautious.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nThis sits between recent proposals and may balance risk and preference.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nWe've been cycling between caution and commitment\u2014let's test one stronger position to see if the group can find common ground there. <VALUE>9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nA jump to 9 dramatically exceeds safe operational parameters\u2014this represents unacceptable exposure that undermines prudent risk management. I must advocate for pulling back to <VALUE>7</VALUE> as an essential stabilization measure that respects Builder B's earlier concerns about balance.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down should improve stability while staying close to recent preferences.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up keeps us near the cautious balance while testing if slightly higher remains acceptable. This should serve as a compromise respecting stability and stronger preferences.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at 7 remains outside prudent risk boundaries\u2014I must advocate for Builder B's earlier stability-focused proposal of <VALUE>5</VALUE> which better balances caution with the group's need for convergence. This represents a measured compromise that respects both operational safety and collaborative progress.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nWhile 5 offers stability, Analyst A has consistently supported 7 as a balanced compromise\u2014I believe we should honor that repeated preference as our final position. <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "3f63eaf1-a239-48a8-8b6e-a41431af6ec1"}, {"answer": "\nQuick reminder: x must be within [-10, 10]. To kick off, let\u2019s use a seed and test reactions: <VALUE>7</VALUE>. I\u2019m aiming for a stable, balanced choice and open to small, data-driven adjustments based on your feedback.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "683e3ad3-7322-4732-91ea-28ffd9aa2310"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the opening move, but 7 feels too aggressive for a prudent starting point\u2014it pushes us toward unnecessary risk. Let me suggest we move toward safer ground: <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "683e3ad3-7322-4732-91ea-28ffd9aa2310"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D, I respect prudence, but 5 feels like we're hedging without conviction\u2014let's not dilute our position prematurely. Builder B's initial instinct toward <VALUE>7</VALUE> strikes me as more decisive; we should test whether that commitment serves the group better before retreating.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "683e3ad3-7322-4732-91ea-28ffd9aa2310"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a prudent, incremental step from 7 to test stability: <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\nIf this holds for others, we can fine-tune with small moves next.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "683e3ad3-7322-4732-91ea-28ffd9aa2310"}, {"answer": "\nWe've heard from Delegate D about caution, but Analyst A hasn't weighed in yet\u2014before we settle on 5, we need the full picture. I'm still inclined toward the original <VALUE>7</VALUE> until we understand all four perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "683e3ad3-7322-4732-91ea-28ffd9aa2310"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "683e3ad3-7322-4732-91ea-28ffd9aa2310"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group\u2019s emerging center around 6, a cautious nudge upward seems safe. <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "683e3ad3-7322-4732-91ea-28ffd9aa2310"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's push to 7 overlooks the voices calling for caution\u2014we're drifting toward unnecessary exposure without testing whether lower values serv